# Rules of Engagement — <Program name>

> Copy to `.umbra/rules.md` and replace every field with the ACTUAL program policy, verbatim
> where possible. Umbra treats this file as binding. If the program prohibits automated
> scanning, do not run Umbra against it.

## Authorization
- Platform / program: <HackerOne | Bugcrowd | Intigriti | self-hosted> — <program URL>
- Policy URL: <link to the program brief you are bound by>
- Enrolled as: <your handle>   (you must be registered and have accepted the terms)
- Automated testing permitted? <YES / NO — quote the policy line>

## In scope (only these)
- <host / domain / CIDR>
- <host / domain / CIDR>
<!-- Enumerate wildcards to concrete hosts. Put these in .umbra/scope.txt too. -->

## Out of scope (never touch)
- <excluded subdomain / third-party service / asset>

## Prohibited actions (quote the policy)
- <e.g. no automated scanning of X, no brute-force, no DoS, no social engineering,
  no testing of payment flows, no accessing other users' data, ...>

## Rate limits / testing constraints
- <e.g. max N requests/second, test during specified windows, ...>

## Required attribution
- Header: <e.g. X-HackerOne-Research: your-handle>   (put in .umbra/bounty.env)

## Disclosure / reporting
- <how and where to submit; do not publicly disclose before resolution, etc.>
